Avoid false failures in CI terminal tests

Check the current Codex screen before waiting for more terminal output.
CI timed out waiting for text that a previous wait had already consumed;
an idle TUI need not produce another update. Preserve the startup loop's
need for fresh output after submitting Enter. A regression test covers
presence and absence waits whose conditions are already satisfied.

Allow two retries per failed test in Linux CI, with a shared budget of
twenty. Limit repeated work on any single failure while leaving room for
unrelated transient failures. Expose the budget through --retry-budget
and consume it atomically so concurrent failures cannot underflow the
counter. Local defaults remain one retry per test and ten across the
suite for faster feedback.

Inspected CI logs show repeated Claude exit failures and recoverable
Kubernetes and SSH flakes, without exhausting the shared retry budget.
Keep these tests enabled while their underlying causes are investigated.
Track the remaining flakes in NVIDIA/rumpelpod#9, #10 and #11.
